WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.752
In their youth, Sun Bin and Pang Juan once studied the art of war together.

00:00:05.102 --> 00:00:08.702
Both were very clever, and both wanted to become famous generals.

00:00:09.052 --> 00:00:13.324
Pang Juan went to Wei first and became a general, but he was jealous of Sun Bin's talent.

00:00:13.674 --> 00:00:16.242
The traditional story says he plotted to frame Sun Bin.

00:00:16.592 --> 00:00:20.024
Only when Sun Bin reached Wei did he realize he had been tricked.

00:00:20.374 --> 00:00:23.422
Later, an envoy of Qi rescued Sun Bin and brought him out.

00:00:23.772 --> 00:00:27.372
Sun Bin came to Qi, where the general Tian Ji recognized his worth.

00:00:27.722 --> 00:00:30.554
Tian Ji hid Sun Bin in his home and protected him.

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:34.672
At the Battle of Guiling, Sun Bin advised striking at Wei's capital.

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:37.950
The Wei army hurried home to rescue it, while the Qi army waited along the road.

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.732
Pang Juan indeed fell into the trap and hurried home with his army.

00:00:42.082 --> 00:00:45.442
At the Battle of Maling, Sun Bin deliberately reduced the number of cooking stoves.

00:00:45.792 --> 00:00:49.224
Pang Juan thought the Qi army was fleeing in fear, and pursued carelessly.

00:00:49.574 --> 00:00:52.646
As the stoves grew fewer, Pang Juan grew more and more pleased with himself.

00:00:52.996 --> 00:00:56.404
Sun Bin was skilled at reading the situation and using the enemy's psychology.

00:00:56.754 --> 00:00:59.562
His military thought has been handed down to today.

00:00:59.912 --> 00:01:02.840
Winning with wisdom matters more than winning with strength.

